{"abstain":false,"answer":"No—if you mean that an incoming request does not match any policy, it is not automatically lost. The system redirects it to the configured HTTPS redirect listener, if present; otherwise, it redirects it to the listener’s default pool. [S6]

The remedy is to check that the intended fallback—your HTTPS redirect listener or default pool—is configured appropriately. You can also adjust policy rules: a policy applies only when all its rules match. Multiple policies can be attached to a listener, but each must have a different priority. [S3][S4][S5]

The supplied documentation does not establish what happens if the fallback destination is unavailable, so it cannot guarantee that all traffic will be successfully served.","citations":["S6","S3","S4","S5"]}
